## Installation

1. Open Zed
2. Run `Extensions > Install Dev Extension`
3. Select the folder for this extension

## Development

### Themes

Edit `themes/<%= id %>.json` to customize colors. See [Zed Theme Documentation](https://zed.dev/docs/themes) for available tokens.

### Languages

Edit `languages/<%= languageId %>/config.toml`.

#### Tree-sitter Grammar

To add syntax highlighting, you'll need a Tree-sitter grammar:

1. Find or create a grammar repo. Try [tree-sitter](https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter)
2. Uncomment and fill in the `[grammars.<%= languageId %>]` section in `extension.toml`
3. Edit the `.scm` files in `languages/<%= languageId %>/`

See [Zed Documentation](https://zed.dev/docs/extensions/languages) for details.

## Publishing

1. Run `zedx version patch|minor|major` to bump the version, then commit and push.
2. Run `zedx publish` to check the extension and print the exact steps for the next one.
3. Open a pull request against [zed-industries/extensions](https://github.com/zed-industries/extensions) that adds this repository as a submodule and adds an entry to `extensions.toml`. For an update, bump the submodule commit and the `version` in `extensions.toml` instead.

See the [Publishing Guide](https://zed.dev/docs/extensions/publishing/publishing-guide) for the full steps and requirements.
